.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="StoichiometricNetwork integrates an arbitrary mass-action reaction network numerically via chemistrykit.integrators. Three classic mechanisms -- built from its named constructors -- are each checked here against a closed-form solution, and the steady-state approximation for the consecutive chain is shown converging as the second step is made much faster than the first.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/kinetics/networks/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_01_reaction_networks_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/kinetics/networks/plot_01_reaction_networks`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Parallel, consecutive, and reversible reaction networks</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/kinetics/networks/plot_01_reaction_networks`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="StoichiometricNetwork&#x27;s general mass-action engine, applied to a three-step radical chain mechanism (initiation, branching propagation, and linear termination), reproduces the qualitative signature of a chain-branching explosion: below a critical branching rate the radical concentration stays small and the fuel decays gently, while above it the radical population grows explosively and burns through the fuel in a short, sharp spike -- exactly the ignition-vs-no-ignition switch behind Semenov&#x27;s and Hinshelwood&#x27;s explosion-limit theory.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/kinetics/networks/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_02_chain_branching_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/kinetics/networks/plot_02_chain_branching`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Chain-branching explosions and Semenov's critical condition</div>
    </div>


